# Run artifacts under results/.
#
# Raw `.bin` samples, compiled CSVs and the per-run EVIDENCE files are
# deliberately NOT ignored: this suite's boundary discipline (README, "No
# number leaves the repo without its harness") requires a reviewed run to
# be committed with everything needed to recompute it — including
# _logs/<cell>_versions.txt (compared-stack version provenance),
# _logs/<cell>_<size>_delivery.txt (delivery accounting), the
# _SHM_UNVERIFIED markers, and the ROS 2 per-size <cell>_<size>_node.log,
# which is the ONLY source for the CSV's `loaned` column
# (compile_csv.py::loaned_from_log). Stage a run explicitly; never with a
# tree-wide `git add`.
#
# What is never committable: the raw per-cell RUN LOGS (regenerable
# console noise, and the AGENTS rule says not to commit them) and the
# smoke gate's scratch directory, which bench.py deletes and rewrites on
# every invocation.
results/**/*.log
!results/**/*_node.log
results/smoke/
# A LIVE workspace run (`cerulion graph run` under workspace/) writes a
# run directory and the flashback plane's rolling window into
# workspace/recordings/. That is per-run scratch the product owns, not
# bench evidence — the bench's evidence is results/ — and it appeared
# untracked after this round's live pod-leg verification.
workspace/recordings/
